{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Projective Module.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Projective Module.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"projective module projective module","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Projective Module.md","fileName":"Projective Module.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Projective Module","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-13 20:00\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Projective Flat and Injective Modules]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Projective Flat and Injective Modules","Free Module","Direct Summand of a Free Module","commutativealgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Projective Module.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Projective Module.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"projective module projective module","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Projective Module.md","fileName":"Projective Module.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Projective Module","heading":"Projective Module","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A projective module P has the lifting property: for every surjection N → M and map P → M, there is a map P → N whose composite is the original map. Maps from P can be lifted across quotients.\n\nEvery [[Free Module]] is projective, and a module is projective exactly when it is a [[Direct Summand of a Free Module]]. Short exact sequences ending in a projective module split.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Projective Flat and Injective Modules","Free Module","Direct Summand of a Free Module","commutativealgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Projective Module.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Projective Module.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"projective module projective module","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Projective Modu